# Command
job-description-cm-commissar = The supreme authority of the bunker. Hands out punishment, makes doctrine and crushes dissent.
job-description-cm-undercommissar = Second in command. Handles day to day operations and enforces the Commissar's will.
job-description-cm-prefect = Low ranking officer overseeing order, discipline and inspections.

# Peacekeeping Corps
job-description-pc-peacekeeper = Frontline enforcer. Responds to conflict, cracks heads, restores order.
job-description-pc-watchman = Stationary guard and patrolman watching corridors and choke points.
job-description-pc-sergeant = Senior peacekeeper commanding squads and coordinating patrols.
job-description-pc-inspector = Interrogator and investigator. Uncovers crimes real or fabricate.

# Labor an Industry
job-description-li-foreman = Supervises labor crews, assigns tasks, and reports failures to Command.
job-description-li-worker = The backbone of the bunker building, repairing, sweating.
job-description-li-machinist = Operates heavy machinery and keeps the production lines running.
job-description-li-turner = Technical specialist who fixes precision parts and maintains tools.
job-description-li-scab = Lowest-class laborer.
job-description-li-janitor = Keeps the facility clean enough to remain habitable.
